From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:39:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max17042_battery: use dSOCi for MAX77759 SOC
 alerts

The MAX77759 fuel gauge has the same Config2.dSOCen / Status.dSOCi
1 % change alert as the MAX17055, and the battery model loaded on POR
enables it (Config2 0x0090 on the Pixel 7 Pro). The driver still
treated the MAX77759 like the older gauges and also armed a SALRT
window of +/-1 % around the current SOC, re-armed from the integer
part of RepSOC on every alert. Both alerts then watch the same
whole-percent boundary.

On a Pixel 7 Pro (gs201) the gauge interrupt fires in bursts of 300
to 460 interrupts within about a second, each time RepSOC crosses a
whole percent, while charging and while discharging; one boot counted
43960 gauge interrupts before the battery ran flat. SALRT read the
window around the new percent (0x1412 at 19.00 %) at every burst.

Use the MAX17055 scheme on the MAX77759: dSOCi for the 1 % steps and
SALRT only for the critical SOC threshold. Google's driver for this
gauge does the same; it enables dSOCen through the model's Config2 and
never programs SALRT. It also drops the 1 % window during suspend, so a
suspended phone is no longer woken on every percent, which is what the
MAX17055 path already does.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
index 7c6ea8e6d..725066381 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
@@ -1193,9 +1193,19 @@ static void max17042_set_critical_soc_threshold(struct max17042_chip *chip)
 		     0xff00 + MAX17042_CRITICAL_SOC : 0xff00);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The MAX17055 and the MAX77759 raise Status.dSOCi on every whole-percent
+ * change of the SOC, so they don't need a SALRT window around the current SOC.
+ */
+static bool max17042_has_dsoci(struct max17042_chip *chip)
+{
+	return chip->chip_type == MAXIM_DEVICE_TYPE_MAX17055 ||
+	       chip->chip_type == MAXIM_DEVICE_TYPE_MAX77759;
+}
+
 static void max17042_enable_soc_alerts(struct max17042_chip *chip)
 {
-	if (chip->chip_type == MAXIM_DEVICE_TYPE_MAX17055) {
+	if (max17042_has_dsoci(chip)) {
 		regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, MAX17055_Config2,
 				   CFG2_DSOCI_BIT_ENBL,
 				   CFG2_DSOCI_BIT_ENBL);
@@ -1208,7 +1218,7 @@ static void max17042_enable_soc_alerts(struct max17042_chip *chip)
 
 static void max17042_suspend_soc_alerts(struct max17042_chip *chip)
 {
-	if (chip->chip_type != MAXIM_DEVICE_TYPE_MAX17055)
+	if (!max17042_has_dsoci(chip))
 		return;
 
 	regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, MAX17055_Config2,
